  "inline_comments": [
    {
      "body": "This might be a little confusing since we are compatible with the libtorch 2.11 ABI. It's really the 2.14 C++ API wrappers that we need 2.14 for. I think something along the lines of \n`# Targets the PyTorch 2.11 stable ABI (requires PyTorch 2.14+ headers at build time) and CPython 3.10 limited API. `\n\nwould be clearer. ",
      "created_at": "2026-11-03T21:34:23Z",
      "diff_hunk": "@@ -36,8 +36,8 @@ else()\n   # fp4_fp4_mega_moe and fused post-expert RMSNorm for Muse Spark Open\n   # (vllm-project/DeepGEMM#39), and the MX MegaMoE alignment fix\n   # (vllm-project/DeepGEMM#43).\n-  # Uses the PyTorch 2.11 stable ABI and CPython 3.10 limited API.\n-  set(_DEEPGEMM_UPSTREAM_TAG \"5cdb145704ec4672ecf4b61441599521ce635df6\")\n+  # Uses the PyTorch 2.14 stable ABI (backwards compatible from PyTorch 2.11) and CPython 3.10 limited API.",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/65494#discussion_r4460705431",
      "id": 4460705431,
      "line": null,
